Here is the question.

What is $$\frac{-\frac{18}{7}}{-\frac{6}{5}}?$$

The options are:
A. \frac{11}{15}
B. \frac{8}{7}
C. \frac{15}{7}
D. \frac{5}{15}

Think the problem through briefly, then end your reply with a final line that reads exactly Answer: X, where X is one of A, B, C or D, with nothing else on that line.

Here is the question.

Select the best translation into predicate logic. Some firefighters rescue victims from danger. (Dx: x is danger; Fx: x is a firefighter; Vx: x is a victim; Rxyz: x rescues y from z)

The options are:
A. (∃x){Fx • (∃y)[Vy • (∃z)(Dz • Rxyz)]}
B. (∀x){Fx ⊃ (∃y)[Vy . (∃z)(Dz • Rxyz)]}
C. (∃x){Fx • (∃y)(∃z)[(Vy • Dz) • Rxzy]}
D. (∀x){Fx ⊃ (∀y)[Vy ⊃ (∃z)(Dz • Rxyz)]}

Think the problem through briefly, then end your reply with a final line that reads exactly Answer: X, where X is one of A, B, C or D, with nothing else on that line.

Here is the question.

Which PyTorch 1.8 command(s) produce $10\times 5$ Gaussian matrix with each entry i.i.d. sampled from $\mathcal{N}(\mu=5,\sigma^2=16)$ and a $10\times 10$ uniform matrix with each entry i.i.d. sampled from $U[-1,1)$?

The options are:
A. \texttt{torch.normal(torch.ones(10,5)*5,torch.ones(5,5)*16)} ; \texttt{(torch.rand(10,10) - 0.5) / 0.5}
B. \texttt{5 + torch.randn(10,5) * 16} ; \texttt{torch.rand(10,10,low=-1,high=1)}
C. \texttt{5 + torch.randn(10,5) * 4} ; \texttt{2 * torch.rand(10,10) - 1}
D. \texttt{torch.normal(torch.ones(10,5)*5,torch.ones(5,5)*16)} ; \texttt{torch.uniform_(10,10,low=-1,high=1)}

Think the problem through briefly, then end your reply with a final line that reads exactly Answer: X, where X is one of A, B, C or D, with nothing else on that line.

